  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food Security and Livelihoods support in Upper Nile</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2023, Fashoda county has seen great improvement in the security situation and stability after the outbreak of violence in 2022. Caritas Malakal has been implementing a resilience project aimed at building the capacities of the communities for self-reliance in Lul and Dethwok payams in Fashoda County since May 2023. This project has supported 1,000 HHs and is ending in March 2024. CDoM plans to maintain its presence in these locations and continue supporting the communities especially in the aftermath of the conflict in Sudan which has significantly increased the number of returnees in these areas. As a result of the Sudan crisis, the hosting communities in these target locations are being overstretched as services are limited and coping capacities are being strained. Fashoda is among the counties in Upper Nile which has transit camps for returnees, and this as also resulted in price increases for staple food.</narrative>
  </description>
